"Destroy target creature.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2024-09-27","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"},{"cmc":0.0,"color_identity":["W"],"colors":[],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"","name":"Plains","oracle_id":"bc71ebf6-2056-41f7-be35-b2e5c34afa99","oracle_text":"({T}: Add {W}.)","power":null,"produced_mana":["W"],"released_at":"2026-11-13","toughness":null,"type_line":"Basic Land — Plains"},{"cmc":3.0,"color_identity":["U"],"colors":["U"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{2}{U}","name":"Propaganda","oracle_id":"ea9709b6-4c37-4d5a-b04d-cd4c42e4f9dd","oracle_text":"Creatures can't attack you unless their controller pays {2} for each creature they control that's attacking you.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2026-06-26","toughness":null,"type_line":"Enchantment"},{"cmc":5.0,"color_identity":["W"],"colors":["W"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"not_legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"not_legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{4}{W}","name":"Sphere of Safety","oracle_id":"92f6c063-a740-4c3c-a60a-569fd298854d","oracle_text":"Creatures can't attack you or planeswalkers you control unless their controller pays {X} for each of those creatures, where X is the number of enchantments you control.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2024-09-27","toughness":null,"type_line":"Enchantment"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"Activating the ability during your opponent’s turn after attackers have been declared will have no effect. The same is true if you activate the ability during your own turn.","oracle_id":"5f358544-7319-4f8e-9d60-a410c4feb774","published_at":"2009-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"After the ability resolves, the targeted creature attacks you only if it’s able to do so as that turn’s declare attackers step begins. If, at that time, the creature is tapped, is affected by a spell or ability that says it can’t attack, or is affected by “summoning sickness,” it can’t attack. If there’s a cost associated with having that creature attack, its controller isn’t forced to pay that cost, so the creature doesn’t have to attack in that case either.","oracle_id":"5f358544-7319-4f8e-9d60-a410c4feb774","published_at":"2009-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the targeted creature would be able to attack either you or a planeswalker you control, it must attack you, not the planeswalker.","oracle_id":"5f358544-7319-4f8e-9d60-a410c4feb774","published_at":"2009-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won't return to the battlefield.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Once the exiled permanent returns, it's considered a new object with no relation to the object that it was. Auras attached to the exiled permanent will be put into their owners' graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled permanent will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled permanent will cease to exist.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The returned card won't be the target of any spells or abilities that targeted it before. Any spells that don't target, such as Akroma's Vengeance, will still affect it.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"When an effect returns the exiled card \"under your control,\" you control it indefinitely after that. In a multiplayer game, if a player leaves the game, all cards that player owns leave as well. If you leave the game, any creatures you control from Cloudshift's effect are exiled.","oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an attacking creature loses haste, perhaps because Fervor leaves the battlefield after attackers have been declared, it won't be removed from combat.","oracle_id":"8e0cea9c-3110-4728-9378-76849e33bb90","published_at":"2012-07-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you control Sphere of Safety, your opponents can choose not to attack with a creature with an ability that says it attacks if able.","oracle_id":"92f6c063-a740-4c3c-a60a-569fd298854d","published_at":"2012-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If there are fewer than twenty cards in the targeted player's library, that player puts all the cards from their library into their graveyard.","oracle_id":"cc2b6e58-2d6f-495e-95f3-9496105c4cba","published_at":"2009-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If there are multiple attacks in a turn, then you have to pay for each attack.","oracle_id":"ea9709b6-4c37-4d5a-b04d-cd4c42e4f9dd","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If there is more than one Propaganda on the battlefield, the cost is cumulative.","oracle_id":"ea9709b6-4c37-4d5a-b04d-cd4c42e4f9dd","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Paying this cost is not an instant or any other kind of ability, it is an additional cost on the declaration of the attacker.","oracle_id":"ea9709b6-4c37-4d5a-b04d-cd4c42e4f9dd","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The payment is made during the declare attackers step at the same time you are declaring the attacker.","oracle_id":"ea9709b6-4c37-4d5a-b04d-cd4c42e4f9dd","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
